A||N||15||FieroFanaticus2||The Ongoing quest for rivets that will work -- Pics!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||07-10-2001||09:05 PM||||So I had nothing to do at work today and decided to look around.  I found a box that said 'Advel - Cherry - Textron' on it.  Remembering that in a different post someone had mentioned that 'Cherry' Rivets would work for attaching the rocker panels after putting on side scoops.  So, I looked around and saw that no one was watching, and I opened the box.  It was a box full of rivets.<BR>Now, for those of you who have put rocker panels back on a fiero, was wondering if you could tell me if these would work or not.  See the pics for size reference.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7100002.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7100006.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||07-10-2001||09:36 PM||||Where are you talking about using then? What part of the rocker panels use rivets?<P><BR>Just did side scoop a while ago and don't remember having to use any rivets.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=12120996&p=43932246&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>I think I did use the plastic push pin type<BR>on the bottoms. Be careful not to crack the glass wiht rivets!! <P>DXR_DAD<p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||07-10-2001||09:57 PM||||I have used collapsing hollow wall anchors with a very short shank on them.  I put them in all the attaching holes for rocker panels, fenders, etc., tightened them down to collapse them and then put JB Weld around them so that they won't ever try to spin as I tighten-loosen the screws.  Now to remove the rocker panels, etc., I just unscrew the appropriate screws.  I am going to do the same thing with the 5 or so fasteners at the the bottom of each outer door panel.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||07-10-2001||10:34 PM||||I used 1/4-20 3/4" long galvanized Pan head screws with nuts.  I painted the heads black.  This allows me to remove a rocker panel easily with out damage.  If I want to remove to the scoops or change the air tube all I need is a screwdriver. I used threaded inserts in the door jambs under the plastic covers. The threaded inserts hold on all the panels where rivets had gone into steel. I had removed all panels for the paint job and didn't use any aluminum rivets just threaded inserts in their place. That way even quarter panels or fenders can be removed by a screwdriver. I only use plastic rivets where they were used previously. Here is where I got the threaded insert rivet kit. <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=1210" TARGET=_blank>http://www.harborfreight.com/cpi/ctaf/Displayitem.taf?itemnumber=1210</A> <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7080039-2_2.jpg">   <BR> <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||bad911||07-11-2001||02:02 AM||||Skitime, what a shot! What a paint job! Truly inspiring. Thanks for the tip too.<P>FieroFanaticus..."A" for effort, but they hafta be 1/4" diameter.<P>I saw some 1/4 x 3/4 plastic push-pin anchors at Menard's today. They might work ok but they were white. This rivet-hunt is a PITA... think I'm gonna go with screws.<p>[This message has been edited by bad911 (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||PJ||07-11-2001||09:27 AM||||Cherry makes hundreds of different types of rivets. The ones you found are nothing like the Klamp-tites. E-mail me your address and I mail you a few of them.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||deceler8||07-11-2001||11:14 AM||||Seems like I've used "Christmas Tree" type fasteners with some luck to hold on rocker panels and the like. They've actually held pretty well, are cheap, and fairly easy to disassemble. They might work with quarters...never tried it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TylerB11||07-11-2001||11:25 AM||||skit time - wow, I must say, I'm breathless. what a picture. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||07-11-2001||07:36 PM||||Here is a thread I started a few weeks ago on that. There are 2 links to companied the specialize in rivits and fasteners <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008317.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008317.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000009||MrPBody||07-11-2001||08:15 PM||||For lower edge of rocker panel: black nylon license plate bolts with a dab of blue Loctite.<P>For rocker panel door sill: black plastic screw rivets (MotorMite / BodyTite).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mark||07-11-2001||10:25 PM||||Skitime, MrPBody, excellent suggestions for rivet replacements.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000011||skitime||07-11-2001||10:42 PM||||bad911 & TylerB11 - Thanks for the compliment on the car.  I posted more pictures of the car in the General Section in the thread "Hey Skitime" if you would like to see more. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroFanaticus2||07-13-2001||08:35 PM||||Ahh Haa!  I found them!!  After searching and putzing around all over the place and much much info from all of you I found them!<BR>It would seem then, that the rocker panels from my car have been removed atleast once before.  Since the rivets that are in there now are the ones that split into a 3-way when set.... these are klamp tites!  And I finally found a place that sells them -- <A HREF="http://www.nicholsindustries.com/fastenerindex.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nicholsindustries.com/fastenerindex.htm</A> <P>I haven't ordered any yet, but plan on it.  I found a site for advel - cherry - textron that sells them as well, but had a hard time navigating their site.  This helps me a lot, maybe it'll help some of you too!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||pherder||07-13-2001||09:13 PM||||I went on the advel - cherry - textron web site and found a distributor in my area ... sort of ...<P>That company's branch store handles the Klamptite rivet but I would have to buy 2000 of them!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I am now going to try FieroFanaticus2's link and see if they will sell to me in small qualities.<P>Hmmmm, they don't show any info on the Klamptites on their web page.<P>Like I wrote, I can get them at a pretty good price ~$0.09 each but have to but minimum of 2000 pieces ($180.00)<P>Anyone want to go in with me?  20 people means 100 rivets each! for $9.00<P>Let's have a Fiero Forum Group Purchase!!!!<P>Paul<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000014||Seanh||07-14-2001||11:34 AM||||Count me in man! My rockers are commin' off soon to be repainted since my red-headed step child took care of them pretty well. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||rockcrawl||07-15-2001||08:48 AM||||Ardel Distributors has just about every fastener you'll ever need for the Fiero. The rivets are a lot more than $.09 each, but you don't have to buy 2000 of them <A HREF="http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ardeldistributors.com/category.html?UCIDs=414669%7C656537</A> ||||reg||1
